// ============================================================================
// at-least-one-probability.epher -- P(at least one success) = 1 - (1-p)^n
//
// If an event has probability p in each of n independent tries, the
// chance it happens at least once is one minus the chance it never
// happens: every try must fail, with probability (1 - p) each, so
//
//   P(at least one) = 1 - (1 - p)^n,
//
// the complement trick of Ross, "A First Course in Probability",
// chapter 2. Adding probabilities instead would be wrong: five tries at
// a 20% event do not add up to a 100% chance, they give 1 - 0.8^5 =
// 2101/3125 = 0.67232.
//
// The script works each case with exact rational powers, so 91/216, for
// instance, is the exact fraction, not an approximation.
//
// Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/probability/distributions/at-least-one-probability.epher"
// Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter
// ============================================================================

// ---- results ----
// A 20% event tried 5 times: exact fraction 2101/3125 = 0.67232.
print("20% event, 5 tries:", 1 - (4/5) ^ 5)
print("as a fraction: 2101/3125")

// Rolling a die, at least one 6 in 3 rolls: 1 - (5/6)^3 = 91/216.
print("at least one 6 in 3 rolls:", 1 - (5/6) ^ 3)

// The classic companion: at least one 6 in 6 rolls is only about 0.665,
// not the 1 that "six chances in six" suggests.
print("at least one 6 in 6 rolls:", 1 - (5/6) ^ 6)
print("exact fraction: 31031/46656")

// A fair coin: at least one head in 10 flips is 1023/1024.
print("at least one head in 10 flips:", 1 - (1/2) ^ 10)

// Two independent 1-in-1000 shots: the double-failure trick scales.
print("1-in-1000 event, 2 tries:", 1 - (999/1000) ^ 2)
// ---- expected output ----
// = 20% event, 5 tries: 0.67232
// = as a fraction: 2101/3125
// = at least one 6 in 3 rolls: 91/216
// = at least one 6 in 6 rolls: 0.66510202332
// = exact fraction: 31031/46656
// = at least one head in 10 flips: 0.9990234375
// = 1-in-1000 event, 2 tries: 0.001999
